From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 104/104] PC5: Games for Windows - LIVE, offline, for the games
 made for it (Wine patch 0906)

A game that imports xlive.dll stopped at the loader, as Wine has no
Games for Windows - LIVE: Resident Evil 5's retail RE5DX10.EXE ended with
"Library xlive.dll not found" (c0000135) before showing anything. A
builtin xlive.dll now has all of xlive 3.5's ordinals, signs in a local
profile so the game saves, and answers every online call as offline. A
game's own xlive.dll (xliveless and its like) is still used first.
